# Intent: two new faces in the mint skin, `listening` (the eyes a little wider and rounder, the mouth a short closed line) and `thinking` (the eyes up and to the right, a small level mouth nudged to that side), so the face carries both states and the ring does not (owner, 2026-11-13). Two new Emotion values (Listening, Thinking) and the names "listening" and "thinking" in SetEmotion; an older firmware logs them as unknown and draws neutral, so the host sends neutral to a unit below the firmware version that has this patch. Sizes in mockup units times 1.35, as the other faces: listening eyes radius 10 (neutral 8, surprised 11), thinking eyes radius 8 offset (+6, -8).
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/ (emotion.h, skins/mint/mint.cpp) and hal/board/stackchan_display.cc (MIT). Applies after 099.
# Check after a flash: say the wake word: the eyes widen and the mouth closes until the answer starts; ask a question that takes a second: the eyes look up to the right with a small mouth; the neutral face returns after the reply. Compare with docs/dev/stackchan-faces-preview-2026-11-13/sheet.png.
diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc b/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc
index edc533a..5c51d6f 100644
--- a/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc
+++ b/firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc
@@ -904,6 +904,10 @@ void StackChanAvatarDisplay::SetEmotion(const char* emotion)
         avatar.setEmotion(Emotion::Surprised);
     } else if (strcmp(emotion, "winking") == 0) {
         avatar.setEmotion(Emotion::Wink);
+    } else if (strcmp(emotion, "listening") == 0) {
+        avatar.setEmotion(Emotion::Listening);
+    } else if (strcmp(emotion, "thinking") == 0) {
+        avatar.setEmotion(Emotion::Thinking);
     } else {
         ESP_LOGW(TAG, "Unknown emotion: %s, using NEUTRAL", emotion);
         avatar.setEmotion(Emotion::Neutral);
